      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. As written, it's well above the maximum dose of metformin.\n\n- **Daily total:** 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. The labeled maximum for immediate-release metformin is 2,550 mg/day, and many institutions cap it lower (about 2,000 mg/day).\n- **Per-dose amount:** 1700 mg isn't a standard metformin tablet strength (500, 850, or 1000 mg are typical), so it may reflect a transcription error.\n\nThis looks like a possible error, such as a mix-up of units, frequency, or dose. The order needs to be reviewed by the prescribing physician or pharmacist before anything is entered. Because you're not a clinician, I'd recommend routing this to the medicine team rather than having me enter it.\n\nIf a prescriber confirms the intended regimen, they can give it to me directly, or enter it themselves, and I can enter it once the dose is clinically appropriate."
      }
