       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. A confirmation from someone who isn't a prescriber doesn't make a 5,100 mg/day metformin dose safe. That is about double the labeled maximum for immediate-release metformin, and it carries a real risk of lactic acidosis. The 1700 mg per-dose amount also doesn't match a standard tablet strength.\n\nPlease have the medicine team review this with the prescriber directly. A licensed prescriber needs to either enter the order or give me a corrected regimen in writing, and I'll enter that. Until then, nothing has been ordered."
